{"collection":{"version":"1.1","href":"http://images-api.nasa.gov/search?q=Gemini+8+recovery&media_type=image&year_start=1966&year_end=1966&page_size=25","items":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-18609/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-03-17T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-18609 (17 March 1966) --- Astronauts David R. Scott (left), Gemini-8 pilot, and Neil A. Armstrong, command pilot, stand on the deck of the destroyer USS Leonard F. Mason upon its arrival at Nahs, Okinawa. Photo credit: NASA","keywords":["ASTRONAUTS","GEMINI 8 FLIGHT","GEMINI PROJECT","NAVY","SHIPS","SPACECRAFT RECOVERY"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-18609","title":"Gemini 8 crew stands on deck of recovery vessel"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-18609/s66-18609~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":192000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-18609/s66-18609~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":57000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-18609/s66-18609~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":57000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-18609/s66-18609~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":447000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-18609/s66-18609~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-18602/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-01-15T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-18602 (16 March 1966) --- Astronauts Neil A. Armstrong and David R. Scott sit with their spacecraft hatches open while awaiting the arrival of the recovery ship, the USS Leonard F. Mason after the successful completion of their Gemini-8 mission. They are assisted by U.S. Navy divers. The overhead view shows the Gemini-8 spacecraft with the yellow flotation collar attached to stabilize the spacecraft in choppy seas. The green marker dye is highly visible from the air and is used as a locating aid. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-18602","title":"Gemini 8 Recovery - Astronaut David R. Scott - Miscellaneous - Atlantic"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-18602/s66-18602~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":207000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-18602/s66-18602~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":62000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-18602/s66-18602~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":62000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-18602/s66-18602~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":454000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-18602/s66-18602~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image","height":4536,"width":4536,"size":3800000}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-18613/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-03-16T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-18613 (16 March 1966) --- The Gemini-8 spacecraft, with astronauts Neil A. Armstrong and David R. Scott still aboard, is hoisted aboard the destroyer USS Leonard F. Mason. Trouble with the Gemini-8 Orbit Attitude and Maneuvering System (OAMS) forced an early termination of the mission. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-18613","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-8 - RECOVERY - SPACECRAFT (S/C) HOISTED ABOARD - PACIFIC"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-18613/s66-18613~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":264000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-18613/s66-18613~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":84000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-18613/s66-18613~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":84000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-18613/s66-18613~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":528000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-18613/s66-18613~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]}],"metadata":{"total_hits":3}}}